      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named for Louis Durant, a Choctaw chief who lived on the site before the 1830s Indian Removal.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durant%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original town layout was surveyed by engineer A., establishing the grid that still guides downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
